{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrwc8Yzg6BTDKbZyVFaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The version-specific `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` settings now work in the START phase. `tests/test_packagesettings.py` and `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py` pass (220 tests). I didn't run lint, format or mypy, because `ruff` and `mypy` aren't in `.venv`. I haven't run the rest of the test suite either.\n\nTwo items you listed were already in the repo, so I only touched their docs. `wheels.get_wheel_server_urls` already took the `version` argument, and `_models.py` already turned a bare `versions:` into an empty mapping. I bumped their `versionadded` and `versionchanged` directives to 0.95.0.\n\n**`_pbi.py`**\n- Both `is_pre_built(version)` and `get_wheel_server_url(version)` strip the local version segment, so `2.8.0+cpu` matches the YAML key `2.8.0`.\n- `is_pre_built(version)` calls the hook through `overrides.find_and_invoke` only when a version is given. The module-level `_default_is_pre_built` returns `None`, and a non-None hook result wins over YAML.\n- The `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` properties now delegate to these two methods with no version.\n\n**`_start.py`**\n- `_re_resolve_url` is added as specified. For source builds it passes `resolver.PYPI_SERVER_URL` as the sdist server, since the bootstrapper doesn't hold one. `get_source_provider` still applies the package's own sdist server override.\n- In the START phase, the re-resolve check runs after `pbi_pre_built` is set. It sits before both the graph add and the has-been-seen check, so the graph stores the final URL and a second parent of an already-seen package still gets its edge.\n- If the new URL can't be found, it logs a WARNING and keeps the original URL.\n\n**Docs**\n- I added short notes to `docs/concepts/package-settings.rst` and `docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst`.\n\n**Tests**\n- Added: local-version lookup, hook only called with a version, a hook result winning over YAML, `None` or omitted `versions` giving an empty mapping, `_re_resolve_url` for the pre-built, source and failure cases, and the START re-resolve behaviour.\n- The START tests check that the graph stores the new URL, the has-been-seen path still re-resolves, a failed re-resolve warns, and nothing re-resolves when the settings match.\n- I changed `test_sets_pbi_pre_built_before_prepare_source` in `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py` to give its mock the `wheel_server_url` fields. Without them the new check saw the mock's URLs as different and tried to re-resolve.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12006,"cache_read_input_tokens":119190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12006},"output_tokens":754,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b768d58-6229-4d6d-b3d9-098d0939ff34","uuid":"a8b2b4c0-786d-4bc2-bf86-9a8a9175360e","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:00:44.176Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrwc8BgFtBe93XN6zRq3"}
